  <language>en_US</language>
  <keyword>ranksum</keyword>
  <short_description>Wilcoxon rank sum test.</short_description>
  <syntax>
    <syntax_item>p = ranksum(x, y)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>p = ranksum(x, y, Name, Value)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>[p, h, stats] = ranksum(...)</syntax_item>
  </syntax>
  <description>
    <p><b>ranksum</b> performs a two-sample rank sum test. <b>NaN</b> observations are omitted from each input vector.</p>
    <p>Name-value arguments include <b>Alpha</b>, <b>Tail</b>, and <b>Method</b>. Supported tails are both, right, and left. Supported methods are auto, exact, and approximate.</p>
  </description>
  <examples>
    <example_item>
      <example_item_type>nelson</example_item_type>
      <example_item_description />
      <example_item_data runnable="cli"><![CDATA[x = [1 3 5];
y = [2 4 6];
[p, h, stats] = ranksum(x, y)]]></example_item_data>
    </example_item>
  </examples>
